## Ambiguities and remaining evidence limits

Evaluate participates in the shared priority cycle. Already-cancelled queued
work consumes a selection turn even when it skips the native call. The shared
cycle starts high on restart. These are explicit decisions where prose leaves
behavior unspecified; no user clarification was requested. Bitmap mapping was
checked empirically against the supplied v1/v2 adapter, without inspecting its
implementation or substituting kernel behavior.

Dispatch is linearized at mutex-protected queue selection. Native calls execute
outside that lock and may enter/finish in another order under OS scheduling.
No external entry/write barrier interposer or scheduler hook was supplied or
added. Exact externally held concurrency and cancellation-boundary qualification
remain unclaimed. Scheduler unit evidence is separate from native-entry evidence.
The predecessor's limitations on whole-service race proof, native diagnostics,
allocation/storage failure injection, simultaneous byte-bound saturation and
power-loss guarantees still apply. Process crashes establish only the tested
histories. Test elapsed times are not workload performance measurements.

The preparation/gate manifest remains absent. The user explicitly authorized
